From: Eugene <eugene@particle.io>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 11:39:17 +0800
Subject: adb: daemon: usb: wait for a UDC before writing the FunctionFS descriptors

While the dual-role port is in host role there is no UDC, so the bind
after the descriptor write fails, ep0 is closed and usb_ffs_open_thread()
retries a second later. Every round writes the descriptors again and
f_fs logs four lines for it ("read descriptors", two bcdVersion warnings,
"read strings"), about once a second for as long as a monitor or a USB
peripheral holds the port in host role: some 330,000 lines a day that
push everything else out of the kernel log. Android does not loop here:
it writes the descriptors once and keeps ep0 open while init has
sys.usb.adb.disabled set. The Linux build drops that property monitor.

Check for the UDC before opening ep0 and leave FunctionFS alone until it
exists, logging once when the wait starts. Device role is unchanged:
once the UDC is back the next round writes the descriptors and binds as
before.

--- a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/usb_ffs.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/usb_ffs.cpp
@@ -280,14 +280,24 @@
     return "";
 }
 
+// The UDC adbd binds to, or "" when it does not exist: a dual-role port has no UDC while it is in
+// host role.
+static std::string PresentUdc() {
+    std::string udc = GadgetUdcName();
+    if (udc.empty() || access(("/sys/class/udc/" + udc).c_str(), F_OK) != 0) {
+        return "";
+    }
+    return udc;
+}
+
 // Returns false when the gadget could not be bound so that the caller backs off before
 // retrying. Binding is synchronous: after the UDC write the controller's "function"
 // attribute names the bound gadget. A failed UDC start (for example a PHY that does not
 // come up) still leaves the driver registered, so the write itself does not report it.
 static bool BindGadgetToUdc() {
-    std::string udc = GadgetUdcName();
-    if (udc.empty() || access(("/sys/class/udc/" + udc).c_str(), F_OK) != 0) {
-        // No UDC while the port is in host role.
+    std::string udc = PresentUdc();
+    if (udc.empty()) {
+        // The port went to host role after open_functionfs() checked.
         LOG(DEBUG) << "no UDC available, gadget not bound";
         return false;
     }
@@ -333,6 +343,24 @@
     v2_descriptor.os_prop_values = os_prop_values;
 
